<node id="mech_atomic_scale_co2rr_understanding">
  <data key="d28">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d29">Explicit consideration of solvent and applied voltage at the electrode–electrolyte interface enables reactive-trajectory and vibrational-signal analysis that provides atomic-scale understanding of the carbon dioxide reduction reaction.</data>
  <data key="d38">atomic_scale_mechanistic_understanding</data>
  <data key="d39">Explicit consideration of solvent and applied voltage at the electrode–electrolyte interface enables reactive-trajectory and vibrational-signal analysis that provides atomic-scale understanding of the carbon dioxide reduction reaction.</data>
  <data key="d40">computational</data>
  <data key="d30">This is the authors' stated interpretation of the operando QM simulation approach and its identification of reactive intermediates.</data>
  <data key="d31">["mech_atomic_scale_co2rr_understanding"]</data>
  <data key="d32">1</data>
  <data key="d33">broad_mechanism_abstract</data>
